          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131634",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z &=3 \\\\ -x+3y &=3 \\\\ -2x-6z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        }
      ],
      ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With Two Pivots"
    },
